		"intro": "This lesson teaches learners how to talk about where they live and where places are located in French. It introduces key questions and answers using “habiter”, prepositions for “in” (à, en, au, aux, dans le), and vocabulary for describing types of places and surroundings. It also develops pronunciation with the nasal vowel sound “in” (as in Singapour, jardin, indien), helping learners speak more naturally when discussing locations and geography.",
		"informationHTML": "<h3>After completing this unit, you will be able to:</h3><ul><li>Ask and answer questions about where people live and where places are located.</li><li>Use key location structures with <em>habiter</em> and <em>se trouver</em> in everyday context.</li><li>Choose the correct French form for “in” (<em>à, en, au, aux, dans le</em>) based on place type and gender.</li><li>Use vocabulary for environment and accommodation (for example <em>à la campagne, en banlieue, dans un immeuble</em>).</li><li>Recognise and produce the nasal vowel sound <em>in</em> in common words and phrases.</li></ul>"
	},
