					"component": "CurrentLocationGrammarPrepositionsInPlaces",
					"id": "grammar1",
					"infoTextHTML": "In this section, you will learn how French expresses location with different forms of <em class='grammar-term-em'>in</em> before place names.<p>You will learn:</p><ul><li>How to choose between <em class='grammar-term-em'>à</em>, <em class='grammar-term-em'>en</em>, <em class='grammar-term-em'>au</em>, <em class='grammar-term-em'>aux</em>, and <em class='grammar-term-em'>dans le</em>.</li><li>How gender, number, and initial sound affect the form used.</li><li>How to apply these forms in real location sentences.</li></ul>",
					"titleTextHTML": "1. Expressing <em class='grammar-term-em'>in</em> with place names"
				}
			}
		],
